.TH LAL_FFTW_WISDOM "1" "January 2026" "LAL" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lal_fftw_wisdom \- a program from LAL
.SH DESCRIPTION
lal_fftw_wisdom \fB\-i\fR INPUT_FILE \fB\-o\fR OUTPUT_FILE [OPTIONS]:
This program creates a wisdom file based on an input file specifying transform
kinds and sizes.  This is much like a simplified version of the fftw\-wisdom
utility provided with FFTW. The transforms to be planned for must be specified
through the input file, one transform per line, using the format:
.IP
<type><direction><size>
.SS "where:"
.TP
<type> is 'r' or 'c'
for real or complex
.TP
<direction> is 'f' or
either 'b' or 'r'  for forward or backward/reverse
.TP
<size>
is the size of the transform
.PP
Backward and reverse are synonymous, and <type> and <direction> are not casesensitive.  For further details and warnings, see the doxygen documentation.
.PP
Options and their behavior are:
.TP
\fB\-\-measurelvl=\fR, \fB\-l\fR <int>
The measurelvl argument to plan creation calls. The
lowest level of zero corresponds to no planning,
whereas the highest level of 3 could take days, depending on the transform size. Defaults to 3.
.TP
\fB\-\-input=\fR, \fB\-i\fR
<file>   Input file containing transforms to plan. Mandatory.
.TP
\fB\-\-output=\fR, \fB\-o\fR <file>
File in which to save generated wisdom. Mandatory.
.TP
\fB\-\-wisdom=\fR, \fB\-w\fR <file>
Existing wisdom file to import. Program exits if this
option is given but the file is unreadable. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-system\-wisdom\fR, \fB\-n\fR By default, system wisdom file \fI\,/etc/fftw/wisdom\/\fP is
imported.  If this option is specified, that import is
disabled.  If the system file is not present or not
readable, a warning is printed but execution continues.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR, \fB\-h\fR
Print this help message and exit.
.PP
In addition to writing the accumulated wisdom to the specified output file, the
program also prints to stdout a human\-readable description of the wisdom successfully created during this invocation.  That description should be appended to the
corresponding description for any wisdom files (including system) read in.
